@{ Layout = null; }
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><title>About &middot; Pakistan Crop Statistics</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content("~/Content/crop-atlas.css")" /><link rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content("~/Content/crop-theme.css")" /><link rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content("~/Content/crop-editorial.css")" /><link rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content("~/Content/crop-shell.css")" /></head>
<body id="page-top" class="crop-shell about-page">@Html.Partial("_CropNavigation")
<main class="workspace" id="main-content"><button id="menu-toggle" class="shell-icon-button dashboard-menu-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Open navigation" aria-controls="crop-navigation" aria-expanded="false"><svg class="shell-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="@Url.Content("~/Content/crop-icons.svg#shell-menu")"></use></svg></button>
<section class="about-intro"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE DASHBOARD</p><h1>Pakistan Crop Statistics</h1><p>Explore the crops that grow across Pakistan, the places that produce them, and how the harvest changes over time.</p><a class="button" href="@Url.Action("Home", "Crops")">Explore the statistics &nearr;</a></section>
<section class="grid about-grid"><article class="panel about-card"><span class="about-number">01</span><h2>Find your perspective</h2><p>Start with the national overview, follow a crop, or explore all reported crops in a province, division, or district.</p><p>Area Comparison puts two places at the same geographic level side by side. Maps, charts, heat tables, and crop detail show their shared strengths and differences.</p><a href="@Url.Action("AreaComparison", "Crops")">Compare two areas &nearr;</a></article><article class="panel about-card"><span class="about-number">02</span><h2>Read the measurements</h2><p>Area and production retain the units and scales reported in the source data. Cotton production must not be interpreted as tonnes.</p><div class="about-formula">Yield = production &divide; area</div><p>Yield is calculated separately for each crop. Missing inputs, incomplete measurements, or zero area produce no yield value. Production across different crops is not combined.</p></article><article class="panel about-card"><span class="about-number">03</span><h2>Understand the geography</h2><p>Some source observations cover combined reporting areas: Karachi (7 districts), Chitral (2 districts), and Kohistan (3 districts).</p><p>These observations remain combined and are not distributed among individual districts. Historical comparisons reflect available records and changes in reporting boundaries.</p></article><article class="panel about-card"><span class="about-number">04</span><h2>Follow progress over time</h2><p>Year-on-year change compares a measurement with the preceding fiscal year. Missing observations or a nonpositive prior-year value produce no percentage comparison.</p><p>The progress heat table supports yield, production, and area. Green indicates an increase; red indicates a decline. Row, column, and table scales adjust color intensity. Averages use valid crop changes only.</p></article></section>
<section class="about-source"><div><p class="eyebrow">DATA SOURCE</p><h2>Pakistan Bureau of Statistics</h2><p>This dashboard presents the crop observations available in its underlying PBS dataset. Availability varies by crop, year, and reporting area.</p></div><a class="quiet" href="https://www.pbs.gov.pk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit PBS &nearr;</a></section>
@Html.Partial("_CropFooter")
</main><script src="@Url.Content("~/Scripts/crop-shell.js")"></script></body></html>
